      },
      "writtenOn": "2025-11-24T10:16:43Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "+CC Alan as well.",
      "parentUuid": "3c9abb41_62e2da91",
      "revId": "0c0827cd395b4153c96698c64b970b45e62f8186",
      "serverId": "dd02978d-1a8e-36d7-bcc0-a5723e5c0abd"
    },
    {
      "unresolved": true,
      "key": {
        "uuid": "8fc3d5a8_258e7286",
        "filename": "src/dawn/native/vulkan/ComputePipelineVk.cpp",
        "patchSetId": 1
      },
      "lineNbr": 111,
      "author": {
        "id": 1002266
      },
      "writtenOn": "2025-11-24T16:01:02Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "The flags allows the implementation to choose the size, but requires it to make it consistent. Without this, the implementation can report a bogus size (which Intel driver would) based on the solely on the limit in the spec. It is varying as opposed to a specific size and different from requiring full subgroups.",
      "parentUuid": "64d5f112_fbf1c8f9",
      "revId": "0c0827cd395b4153c96698c64b970b45e62f8186",
      "serverId": "dd02978d-1a8e-36d7-bcc0-a5723e5c0abd"
    },
    {
      "unresolved": true,
      "key": {
        "uuid": "38b1f0e3_45198545",
        "filename": "src/dawn/native/vulkan/ComputePipelineVk.cpp",
        "patchSetId": 1
      },
      "lineNbr": 111,
      "author": {
        "id": 1000002
      },
      "writtenOn": "2025-11-24T16:43:27Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "I finally read https://registry.khronos.org/vulkan/specs/latest/html/vkspec.html#interfaces-builtin-variables-sgs and ... that enum name is supremely confusing. However I still have a concern that skipping `VK_PIPELINE_SHADER_STAGE_CREATE_ALLOW_VARYING_SUBGROUP_SIZE_BIT` will cause issues because I can imagine how a shader might inadvertently rely on the subgroup size to be uniform in a dispatch, even without using the builtin. And AFAIK WGSL requires the subgroups to all be the same size in a single dispatch, even if subgroup size isn\u0027t used.",
      "parentUuid": "8fc3d5a8_258e7286",
      "revId": "0c0827cd395b4153c96698c64b970b45e62f8186",
      "serverId": "dd02978d-1a8e-36d7-bcc0-a5723e5c0abd"
    },
    {
      "unresolved": true,
      "key": {
        "uuid": "6fc2ba9a_3ebf79bd",
        "filename": "src/dawn/native/vulkan/ComputePipelineVk.cpp",
        "patchSetId": 1
      },
      "lineNbr": 111,
      "author": {
        "id": 1002266
      },
      "writtenOn": "2025-11-24T19:28:25Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "Agreed with Corentin. If we need to set a specific size, we should instead make an experimental feature for that.",
      "parentUuid": "38b1f0e3_45198545",
      "revId": "0c0827cd395b4153c96698c64b970b45e62f8186",
      "serverId": "dd02978d-1a8e-36d7-bcc0-a5723e5c0abd"
    },
    {
      "unresolved": true,
      "key": {
        "uuid": "1534bde5_ff5b7644",
        "filename": "src/dawn/native/vulkan/ComputePipelineVk.cpp",
        "patchSetId": 1
      },
      "lineNbr": 111,
      "author": {
        "id": 1000019
      },
      "writtenOn": "2025-11-25T03:12:50Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "Do you think we can have an extension to specify the required subgroup size now? We can also support it on D3D12 with Shader Model 6.6 (https://microsoft.github.io/DirectX-Specs/d3d/HLSL_SM_6_6_WaveSize.html).\n\nAt least we should fix the implementation here as it violates Vulkan SPEC. When we use `subgroupSizeInfo.requiredSubgroupSize` we shouldn\u0027t set `VK_PIPELINE_SHADER_STAGE_CREATE_ALLOW_VARYING_SUBGROUP_SIZE_BIT`. What do you think?",
      "parentUuid": "6fc2ba9a_3ebf79bd",
      "revId": "0c0827cd395b4153c96698c64b970b45e62f8186",
      "serverId": "dd02978d-1a8e-36d7-bcc0-a5723e5c0abd"
    },
    {
      "unresolved": true,
      "key": {
        "uuid": "c961b78b_6ded7ca8",
        "filename": "src/dawn/native/vulkan/ComputePipelineVk.cpp",
        "patchSetId": 1
      },
      "lineNbr": 111,
      "author": {
        "id": 1002266
      },
      "writtenOn": "2025-11-25T04:21:40Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "The varying bit and required sizes are alternatives. Both consistent subgroup sizes. So I can see a couple cases:\n1. Behind the scenes on specific HW we want a specific size. In this case don\u0027t set the varying bit, but add the required subgroup size.\n2. Allow users to specify a subgroup size between min and max from the adapter. This would be an experimental extension. It could be implemented on D3D12 and Vulkan (not Metal though).",
      "parentUuid": "1534bde5_ff5b7644",
      "revId": "0c0827cd395b4153c96698c64b970b45e62f8186",
      "serverId": "dd02978d-1a8e-36d7-bcc0-a5723e5c0abd"
    },
    {
      "unresolved": true,
      "key": {
        "uuid": "a17f10a0_66c63166",
